      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "cccc1a80f91f780817604eae7246bd8d91c8c147",
            "subject": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: release the pools of an old HCA"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-09 15:38:44.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-16 18:10:29.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: drop the CM conn ref one time",
        "message": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: drop the CM conn ref one time\n\nA cm_id holds a ref on its conn. The CM handler and\nkiblnd_abort_connreq() both drop that ref. Only the DISCONNECTED\npath clears cmid->context, so a later event can drop the ref again.\n\nAdd kiblnd_cm_conn_put(). It drops the ref only if its cmpxchg()\nclears cmid->context.\n\nA passive conn in IBLND_CONN_PASSIVE_WAIT is not on ibp_connreqs,\nso connd never times it out. With no CM event, the conn and its\ncm_id stay. Put the passive conn on ibp_connreqs after rdma_accept().\nA CM event claims the connreq before it uses the conn. So connd and\nthe CM handler cannot both complete one connreq.\n\nFixes: 0b8c18d8c863 (\"LU-17480 o2iblnd: add a timeout for rdma_connect\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ia1493fc1ed5b006fe44d9c6ae2813da7ce238352\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
